---
import Code from 'slides/Code';
const mac = `xcode-select --install`;
const wsl = `sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y clang git`;
const gpu = `brew install llvm@21
echo "export LLVM_PATH=$(brew --prefix llvm@21)/lib/libLLVM.dylib" >> ~/.zshrc`;
const uv = `curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh`;
---
<header>
  <div class="section">your machine · 1 of 2</div>
  <h2>install the tools</h2>
  <p class="sub">open a terminal: <b>Terminal</b> on a mac, <b>Ubuntu</b> (wsl) on windows. click a box's copy button, paste, press enter</p>
</header>
<div class="s11">
  <div class="os">
    <h3>mac</h3>
    <Code lang="sh" code={mac} copy />
    <p>a window pops up: click <b>install</b>. gives you <code>clang</code> (a c compiler) and <code>git</code>. if it says they're already installed, you're done</p>
  </div>
  <div class="os">
    <h3>windows (wsl) and linux</h3>
    <Code lang="sh" code={wsl} copy />
    <p>it asks for the password you made for ubuntu. typing it shows nothing; that's normal</p>
  </div>
  <div class="gpu">
    <h3>mac, for the gpu (Metal): llvm from homebrew</h3>
    <Code lang="sh" code={gpu} copy />
    <p>then <b>open a new terminal</b>. no <code>brew</code>? install homebrew from <b>brew.sh</b> first. without llvm, everything still runs on the cpu, just slower</p>
  </div>
  <div class="both">
    <h3>both: uv, which installs python and python packages</h3>
    <Code lang="sh" code={uv} copy />
    <p>then <b>close the terminal and open a new one</b>, so it finds <code>uv</code>. check: <code>uv --version</code></p>
  </div>
</div>
<style>
  .s11 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px 56px; font-size: .62em; width: 100%; }
  .s11 h3 { color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 .3em; font-size: 1.05em; }
  .s11 p { margin: .45em 0 0; color: var(--muted); }
  .s11 p b, .s11 p code { color: var(--fg); }
  .s11 .both, .s11 .gpu { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .s11 :global(pre.code) { font-size: 1em; }
</style>
